@node INTRO "Introduction"
@{b}Introduction@{ub}

Beam68 is a Spotlight/Launchy-style launcher.  Press a hotkey anywhere,
type a few letters of a program, document, drawer or game, and press
Enter.

It is written for real Amiga hardware: one program runs on every CPU from
the 68000 to the 68060, it needs no MUI, ReAction, FPU or TCP/IP stack,
it uses little memory, and it indexes your drawers in the background
without slowing down the machine.

Beam68 consists of:

  @{b}Beam68@{ub}        the resident launcher (a Commodity)
  @{b}Beam68Prefs@{ub}   the settings program in SYS:Prefs
  @{b}Beam68Ctl@{ub}     a Shell tool to control the launcher
  @{b}Plugins@{ub}       small programs started from the search field

@endnode

@node REQUIREMENTS "Requirements"
@{b}Requirements@{ub}

  @{b}AmigaOS 3.0@{ub} or newer (Kickstart 39).  AmigaOS 3.2 is
  recommended.

  @{b}Any 680x0 CPU@{ub}.  A 68020 or faster with Fast RAM is recommended
  for large indexes; a 68000 works fine with the default settings.

  @{b}Memory@{ub}: about 300 KB for the resident launcher with the default
  512-entry index.

Optional:

  workbench.library V44+ (OS 3.1.4, 3.5, 3.9, 3.2) to open drawers from
  results.  On 3.0/3.1, programs, projects and games still start.

  The @{b}Installer@{ub} utility for the graphical installation (part of
  OS 3.1 and later; Installer 43.3 for 3.0 is on Aminet).

  @{b}C:LhA@{ub} or @{b}C:UnZip@{ub} (Aminet) to install plugin archives.

  @{b}WHDLoad@{ub} for game support.

@endnode

@node INSTALL "Installation"
@{b}Installation, update and removal@{ub}

Double-click the @{b}Install@{ub} icon.  The Installer asks what to do:

@{b}Install or update@{ub}

  Choose the drawer in which the Beam68 drawer is created (default
  SYS:Utilities), the plugins to install and whether Beam68 starts with
  Workbench.  Beam68Prefs always goes to SYS:Prefs.

  An update stops a running launcher first, keeps all your settings in
  ENVARC:Beam68 and your icons, adds newly chosen plugins to your
  configuration and leaves third-party plugins alone.

@{b}Uninstall@{ub}

  Removes the Beam68 drawer (including all plugins), Beam68Prefs and the
  startup entry, and asks whether to keep your settings.

The chosen drawer is remembered in ENVARC:Beam68/InstallDir.  For
scripted installs use the Shell installer: @{b}Execute scripts/Install-Beam68@{ub}.

@endnode

@node FIRSTSTEPS "First steps"
@{b}First steps@{ub}

Start Beam68 (it starts automatically with Workbench if you chose so).
No window opens: Beam68 waits in the background.

Press @{b}Ctrl+Alt+Space@{ub}.  The launcher opens on the screen you are
working on.  Type @{i}multi@{ui} and press Enter to start MultiView.

The first start indexes SYS:Tools, SYS:Utilities, SYS:Prefs and
SYS:System.  This runs in the background and is saved, so later starts
are instant.  Add your own drawers, such as Work: or Games:, on the
@{"Indexing page" link PREFS_INDEXING} of Beam68Prefs.

Press the hotkey again or Esc to close the launcher.

@endnode

@node SEARCH "Searching"
@{b}Searching@{ub}

Beam68 finds a program by:

  the exact name               @{i}ed@{ui}       finds Ed
  the start of the name        @{i}multi@{ui}    finds MultiView
  the start of a word          @{i}paint@{ui}    finds Deluxe Paint
  initial letters              @{i}dp@{ui}       finds Deluxe Paint
  any part of the name         @{i}view@{ui}     finds MultiView
  one typing mistake           @{i}scren@{ui}    finds ScreenMode
  several words                @{i}paint lux@{ui} finds Deluxe Paint
  aliases and keywords you added in Beam68Prefs

The letters that matched are underlined in the results.

Pinned favorites (F6) and frequently launched programs rank a little
higher.  With @{b}QUICK_LAUNCH=control alt@{ub} in the configuration,
Ctrl+Alt+1 ... 9 start favorites 1-9 from anywhere.  With an empty search field the launcher shows your favorites
and recently used programs.

@endnode

@node SCOPES "Search scopes"
@{b}Search scopes@{ub}

Start the query with a scope to search only one kind of result:

  @{b}app:@{ub}      tools and executables
  @{b}file:@{ub}     indexed files (enable Files on the Indexing page)
  @{b}drawer:@{ub}   drawers
  @{b}game:@{ub}     WHDLoad games, see @{"WHDLoad games" link WHDLOAD}
  @{b}volume:@{ub}   mounted volumes and assigns, read live from DOS
  @{b}doc:@{ub}      documents you opened through Beam68 (last 16)
  @{b}hidden:@{ub}   results you hid with Shift+Del
  @{b}mod:@{ub}      music modules (INDEX_MODULES=YES)
  @{b}web:@{ub}      browser bookmarks (BOOKMARK_FILES)
  @{b}snip:@{ub}     text snippets; Enter copies the text
  @{b}script:@{ub}   ARexx scripts in REXX:
  @{b}prefs:@{ub}    the preference programs in SYS:Prefs
  @{b}stats:@{ub}    your most-launched programs with their counts
  @{b}recent:@{ub}   programs you launched before
  @{b}fav:@{ub}      favorites; @{i}fav:games@{ui} shows the group "games"
  @{b}plugin:@{ub}   plugin examples and help

@endnode

@node KEYS "Keyboard"
@{b}Launcher keys@{ub}

  Ctrl+Alt+Space    open or close (changeable in Preferences)
  Enter             launch the selected result
  Up / Down         select a result
  Shift+Up/Down     a page at a time (also PageUp/PageDown)
  Ctrl+Up/Down      first / last result (also Home/End)
  Tab               accept a completion, or cycle the result action
  Ctrl+L or Ctrl+U  clear the search
  Amiga+V           paste the first clipboard line
  Ctrl+1 ... Ctrl+9 start favorite 1-9 (in pin order)
  Mouse wheel       select a result
  Shift+Del         hide the selected result (in hidden: show it again)
  Right             on a drawer result (cursor at the end): browse it
  Left              while browsing (cursor at the start): parent drawer
  F1 or Help        searchable list of commands, plugins and keys
  F2                update the index (results stay usable)
  Shift+F2          rebuild the index from scratch
  F3 / Shift+F3     reload settings / reload plugins only
  F4                quit Beam68
  F5                open Beam68Prefs
  F6                pin or unpin the selected result as a favorite
  F7 / Shift+F7     older / newer query history
  F8                recall the last shell command
  Esc               cancel a running plugin, or close the launcher

@endnode

@node ACTIONS "Result actions"
@{b}Result actions@{ub}

Press @{b}Tab@{ub} on a result to cycle its action, then Enter:

  @{b}Launch@{ub}          start it (default)
  @{b}Run with arguments@{ub}  type arguments, Enter runs the program in a
                  console (needs Built-in Shell Commands)
  @{b}Open drawer@{ub}     open the drawer that contains it
  @{b}Show in Directory Opus@{ub}  open the drawer in an Opus lister (only
                  offered while Directory Opus 4/5 or Magellan runs)
  @{b}Information@{ub}     Workbench's Information window
  @{b}Copy path@{ub}       put the path on the clipboard
  @{b}custom action@{ub}   defined on the Applications page of Beam68Prefs,
                  e.g. "Edit" with the command @{i}C:Ed {path}@{ui}

@{b}{path}@{ub} and @{b}{drawer}@{ub} are replaced by the quoted path of the
result and of its drawer.

@endnode

@node BROWSE "Browsing drawers"
@{b}Browsing drawers@{ub}

Select a drawer or volume result and press @{b}Right@{ub} (with the cursor at
the end of the search text).  The launcher lists that drawer: drawers
first, then files.  Type to filter, Enter opens a file or enters a drawer,
@{b}Left@{ub} (cursor at the start) goes to the parent, Esc returns to the
normal search.  Browsing reads the drawer directly; it does not need the
drawer to be indexed.

@endnode

@node SHELL "Shell commands"
@{b}Shell commands@{ub}

Type @{b}shell:@{ub} or simply @{b}>@{ub} followed by an AmigaDOS command:

  >dir SYS:
  shell:list RAM: ALL

The output appears in a console window that closes after success and
waits when there is something to read.  F8 recalls the last command.

Because this runs any command, it can be switched off on the Plugins page
of Beam68Prefs (@{b}Built-in Shell Commands@{ub}).

@{b}restart workbench@{ub} and @{b}restart amiga@{ub} restart the Workbench or
the whole computer; both need a second Enter.

@endnode

@node SOURCES "More index sources"
@{b}Modules, bookmarks, snippets and scripts@{ub}

@{b}Music modules@{ub}  With INDEX_MODULES=YES, MOD/MED/XM/S3M/IT/AHX and
similar files (mod.name or name.mod) in the indexed drawers become MOD
results.  If the player is already running (its ARexx port, by default
HIPPOPLAYER, exists) Enter sends it the module with the Player ARexx
command, by default LOAD "{file}", so no second copy starts.  Otherwise
MODULE_COMMAND starts the player, by default Run >NIL: HippoPlayer
"{file}".  For other players set the port and command from their ARexx
documentation.  Add your music drawer as a directory.

@{b}Bookmarks@{ub}  BOOKMARK_FILES lists hotlist files separated by ';'.
Any layout is read: HTML with one or several links per line or links
spread over lines (NetSurf, IBrowse and AWeb HTML exports), and plain text
files with bare http:// addresses, which take the text before the address
as their title.  Enter opens a bookmark with URL_COMMAND, by default
OpenURL "{url}" (the OpenURL package on Aminet sends it to your browser).

@{b}Snippets@{ub}  ENVARC:Beam68/Snippets.txt holds name<TAB>text lines.
Enter copies the text to the clipboard; paste it with Amiga+V.

@{b}ARexx scripts@{ub}  Every .rexx in REXX: is indexed (INDEX_REXX) and
runs with RX in a console window.

@{b}Preferences@{ub}  prefs: always lists the programs in SYS:Prefs, read
directly when you search, even if SYS:Prefs is not an indexed drawer.

All of these are set on the @{"Sources page" link PREFS_SOURCES} of Beam68Prefs.

These sources are read on a full index update: F2 picks up new and
removed entries; after changing an existing snippet's text or a bookmark's
title press Shift+F2 (complete rebuild).

@endnode

@node WHDLOAD "WHDLoad games"
@{b}WHDLoad games@{ub}

Beam68 recognises WHDLoad installations in the drawers it indexes:

  @{b}Game icons@{ub} whose Default Tool is WHDLoad - the normal way a
  WHDLoad game is installed - appear as @{b}GAME@{ub} results and start
  exactly as if you had double-clicked the icon, with all its tool types.

  @{b}.slave files@{ub} without such an icon also appear.  They are started
  with @{i}WHDLoad SLAVE=<slave> DATA=<drawer> PRELOAD@{ui}.

Beam68 reads each game's real title and copyright from its slave, so
"final fight" finds TurricanII, and shows it next to the result.  If the
game needs a Kickstart image that is missing from DEVS:Kickstarts, Beam68
says so; press Enter again to start it anyway.  @{b}game:random@{ub} picks a
game for you.

To use it, add your games drawer (for example Games: or Work:Games) on the
@{"Indexing page" link PREFS_INDEXING} and keep @{b}WHDLoad games@{ub} ticked.
A depth of 3 or 4 covers the usual Games/A/Name/ layout.  Type
@{b}game:@{ub} to search only games.

Configuration: @{b}INDEX_GAMES=YES|NO@{ub} and @{b}WHDLOAD_COMMAND=@{ub}
(default "WHDLoad", found through the Shell path; use C:WHDLoad or a full
path if needed).

@endnode

@node PLUGINS "Plugins"
@{b}Plugins@{ub}

Plugins are small programs you start from the search field with a
trigger character or a readable prefix, then Enter:

  @{b}=@{ub}  Calculator          =12*(3+4), =$FF+%1010 (hex/binary)
  @{b}\@@{ub}  Clock               \@
  @{b}?@{ub}  Memory              ?
  @{b}/@{ub}  File Finder         find:readme
  @{b}!@{ub}  System Commands     system:avail, reboot confirm
  @{b}#@{ub}  Assigns and Volumes dos:assigns, diskfree:RAM:
  @{b}^@{ub}  Task Manager        tasks, task:break:name:confirm
  @{b}&@{ub}  Clipboard Tools     clip:show, clip:upper
  @{b}:@{ub}  Date Utilities      date:add:7, date:weekday:2026-12-24
  @{b}~@{ub}  Workbench Windows   windows, window:shell
  @{b}$@{ub}  Developer Tools     dev:hex:255, dev:prot:RWED
  @{b}%@{ub}  ARexx Runner        rexx:list
  @{b}|@{ub}  Music Controls      music:next, music:volume 50

Some plugins answer with a list: File Finder, for example, shows up to
eight matches.  Select one and press Enter to open it; Esc goes back.

The calculator accepts $FF or 0xFF (hexadecimal) and %1010 (binary) and
shows every result in decimal, hexadecimal and, up to 65535, binary.

@{b}PLUGIN_CACHE=YES@{ub} copies each plugin to T:Beam68/PluginCache the first
time it runs and starts it from RAM afterwards - much faster on a floppy
or slow CompactFlash.  (True "resident" programs must be re-entrant, which
ordinary plugins are not, so each run still starts a fresh copy.)

Press F1 in the launcher for the full list with examples.  Plugins marked
@{b}SYSTEM@{ub} ask for a second Enter.  A plugin that fails three times in
a row is quarantined until you enable it again in Beam68Prefs.

@endnode

@node PACKAGES "Plugin packages"
@{b}Plugin packages@{ub}

Every plugin is a drawer under Beam68/Plugins/ with a .plugin manifest,
the program and any extra files.  Third-party plugins are distributed as
.lha or .zip archives containing such a drawer.

To install one, open the @{"Plugins page" link PREFS_PLUGINS} of Beam68Prefs and
drop the archive (or an unpacked plugin drawer) on the window, or type or
Browse its path and click @{b}Add@{ub}.  Beam68Prefs shows the plugin's
author, version, licence and what it may access, and asks before
installing.  A newer version of an installed plugin replaces it.

Beam68Prefs reads the contents of LHA archives itself and refuses unsafe
paths before anything is unpacked.  Archives are unpacked with
@{b}C:LhA@{ub} or @{b}C:UnZip@{ub}.  Without them,
unpack the archive yourself and install the drawer.

@{b}Remove@{ub} takes a plugin off the list and can also delete its files.

Plugins can also be written in ARexx: a package whose COMMAND is a .rexx
script runs through RX (RexxMast must be running).  Some plugins show
their answer while you type (live preview), for example dev:hex:255.

The catalogue (Extras page) lists plugins and themes published as a
simple index file; select one and choose Install.

Writing plugins: see the @{b}Beam68PluginSDK.guide@{ub} in the SDK archive.

@endnode

@node PREFS "Preferences"
@{b}Beam68Prefs@{ub}

Open SYS:Prefs/Beam68Prefs, or press F5 in the launcher.  The pages:

  @{" General       " link PREFS_GENERAL}
  @{" Indexing      " link PREFS_INDEXING}
  @{" Plugins       " link PREFS_PLUGINS}
  @{" Appearance    " link PREFS_APPEARANCE}
  @{" Favorites     " link PREFS_FAVORITES}
  @{" Applications  " link PREFS_APPLICATIONS}
  @{" Accessibility " link PREFS_ACCESSIBILITY}
  @{" Extras        " link PREFS_EXTRAS}
  @{" Sources       " link PREFS_SOURCES}

@{b}Use@{ub} applies the settings until reboot, @{b}Save@{ub} keeps them,
@{b}Cancel@{ub} discards changes.  F7/F8 or Left/Right switch pages; the
Help key opens this manual at the current page.

@endnode

@node PREFS_GENERAL "Preferences: General"
@{b}General@{ub}

  @{b}Hotkey@{ub}        click Capture... and press the new key combination
  @{b}Launcher@{ub}      shows whether Beam68 runs; Start (F9), Restart
                (Shift+F9) and Stop (F10)
  @{b}Results, size@{ub} number of visible results and window size
  @{b}History@{ub}       learn from launches to rank programs
  @{b}Index cache@{ub}   save the index so starting is instant

@{"Back to Preferences" link PREFS}
@endnode

@node PREFS_INDEXING "Preferences: Indexing"
@{b}Indexing@{ub}

  @{b}Directories@{ub}   the drawers that are searched (drop drawers here)
  @{b}Depth@{ub}         how many levels of sub-drawers are searched
  @{b}Icons@{ub}         index Workbench tools and projects
  @{b}Executables@{ub}   index programs without icons (slower to scan)
  @{b}Files@{ub}         index plain files (uses many index entries)
  @{b}Drawers@{ub}       index drawers
  @{b}WHDLoad games@{ub} index WHDLoad games, see @{"WHDLoad games" link WHDLOAD}
  @{b}File patterns@{ub} which files are indexed, e.g. *.guide,*.txt
  @{b}Excluded@{ub}      drawers to skip, separated by ;

Changes to drawers are noticed automatically; F2 rebuilds the whole index.

@{"Back to Preferences" link PREFS}
@endnode

@node PREFS_PLUGINS "Preferences: Plugins"
@{b}Plugins@{ub}

The list shows every plugin with its trigger.  Select one and use
@{b}Details@{ub} (what it is and may access), @{b}Settings@{ub},
@{b}Enable/Disable@{ub}, @{b}Up/Down@{ub} (order) and @{b}Remove@{ub}.

Install third-party plugins by dropping their archive on the window - see
@{"Plugin packages" link PACKAGES}.  With a plugin selected, the Help key
opens that plugin's own guide if it has one.

@{b}Timeout@{ub} is how long the launcher waits for a plugin.
@{b}Export report@{ub} writes RAM:Beam68-Diagnostics.txt.
@{b}Built-in Shell Commands@{ub} enables shell: and >.

@{"Back to Preferences" link PREFS}
@endnode

@node PREFS_APPEARANCE "Preferences: Appearance"
@{b}Appearance@{ub}

Choose the Workbench colours, one of four Catppuccin-inspired themes or
your own colours.  @{b}Edit colours...@{ub} opens red/green/blue sliders for
each colour of the custom theme.  More themes are in Beam68/Themes and in
the plugin catalogue; load one with Theme file -> Import.  Changes are previewed in the open launcher.  Themes can
be exported to and imported from .theme files.  On screens with few
colours Beam68 falls back to the Workbench colours.

@{"Back to Preferences" link PREFS}
@endnode

@node PREFS_FAVORITES "Preferences: Favorites"
@{b}Favorites@{ub}

Favorites appear first when the search field is empty.  Each has a group,
so @{b}fav:games@{ub} lists only the "games" group.  Add programs by
dropping their icons here, or press F6 on a result in the launcher.

@{"Back to Preferences" link PREFS}
@endnode

@node PREFS_APPLICATIONS "Preferences: Applications"
@{b}Applications@{ub}

Give programs extra search words (aliases), for example "paint graphics"
for Deluxe Paint, and an optional custom action with a label and a
command; see @{"Result actions" link ACTIONS}.

@{"Back to Preferences" link PREFS}
@endnode

@node PREFS_ACCESSIBILITY "Preferences: Accessibility"
@{b}Accessibility@{ub}

  @{b}Launcher font@{ub}  any font from FONTS: (Choose... opens a requester)
  @{b}Row spacing@{ub}    space between result rows
  @{b}High-contrast@{ub}  selection drawn in the Workbench fill colours
  @{b}Larger gadgets@{ub} for Beam68Prefs
  @{b}Reduced colors@{ub} never allocate theme colours
  @{b}Compact@{ub}        smaller launcher on low-resolution screens

@{"Back to Preferences" link PREFS}
@endnode

@node PREFS_EXTRAS "Preferences: Extras"
@{b}Extras@{ub}

  @{b}Favorite keys@{ub}    qualifiers for global favorite keys, e.g.
                   "control alt" gives Ctrl+Alt+1 ... 9 (empty = off)
  @{b}WHDLoad command@{ub}  how icon-less .slave files are started
  @{b}Opus ARexx port@{ub}  Directory Opus port, normally DOPUS.1
  @{b}Open drawers in Directory Opus@{ub}  while Opus runs
  @{b}Run plugins from a RAM copy@{ub}  faster on floppy or slow CF
  @{b}Results kept@{ub}     8-64 results that can be scrolled
  @{b}Browse entries@{ub}   16-512 entries listed when browsing a drawer
  @{b}Hidden max@{ub}       1-256 results you can hide
  @{b}Recent docs@{ub}      1-64 documents remembered for doc:
  @{b}Export/Import preset@{ub}  save or load a complete setup (settings,
                   favorites, aliases, hidden results, plugin settings) as
                   one .preset file
  @{b}Plugin catalogue@{ub}  browse and install plugins and themes from a
                   catalogue index (URL or file).  Downloads use
                   DOWNLOAD_COMMAND, by default wget from Aminet.

@{"Back to Preferences" link PREFS}
@endnode

@node PREFS_SOURCES "Preferences: Sources"
@{b}Sources@{ub}

  @{b}Index music modules@{ub}  modules in the indexed drawers (mod:)
  @{b}Player port@{ub}          ARexx port of a running player (HIPPOPLAYER)
  @{b}Player ARexx@{ub}         command sent to it, {file} = the module
  @{b}Start player@{ub}         command when the player is not running
  @{b}Index ARexx scripts@{ub}  scripts in REXX: (script:)
  @{b}Bookmark files@{ub}       hotlists, ';'-separated; Browse adds one
  @{b}Open URL with@{ub}        command for bookmarks, {url} = the address

See @{"More index sources" link SOURCES}.

@{"Back to Preferences" link PREFS}
@endnode

@node CONFIG "Configuration file"
@{b}Configuration@{ub}

Settings are plain text: ENV:Beam68/Beam68.cfg (current) and
ENVARC:Beam68/Beam68.cfg (saved).  Beam68Prefs edits them for you; after a
manual edit press F3 in the launcher.

  HOTKEY=rawkey control alt space
  DIR=SYS:Tools               (repeat for each drawer)
  EXCLUDE_DIR=SYS:Trashcan    (repeat)
  MAX_DEPTH=4                 MAX_ITEMS=512
  SCAN_ICONS=YES              SCAN_EXECUTABLES=NO
  INDEX_FILES=NO              INDEX_DRAWERS=YES
  INDEX_GAMES=YES             WHDLOAD_COMMAND=WHDLoad
  QUICK_LAUNCH=control alt    (optional: global keys for favorites 1-9)
  DOPUS_PORT=DOPUS.1          OPEN_DRAWERS_IN_DOPUS=NO
  PLUGIN_CACHE=NO             (YES: run plugins from a RAM copy)
  RESULTS_MAX=32  BROWSE_MAX=128  HIDDEN_MAX=32  RECENT_DOCS=16
  CATALOGUE_URL=http://...    DOWNLOAD_COMMAND=wget -q -O "{file}" "{url}"
  INDEX_REXX=YES  INDEX_MODULES=NO  BOOKMARK_FILES=a.html;b.html
  MODULE_COMMAND=Run >NIL: HippoPlayer "{file}"   URL_COMMAND=OpenURL "{url}"
  MODULE_PORT=HIPPOPLAYER     MODULE_AREXX=LOAD "{file}"
  FILE_PATTERNS=*             INDEX_CACHE=YES
  HISTORY=YES                 SHELL_COMMANDS=YES
  VISIBLE_RESULTS=6           WINDOW_WIDTH=550   WINDOW_HEIGHT=0
  THEME=WORKBENCH             CUSTOM_COLORS=CDD6F4,585B70,F38BA8,1E1E2E,11111B
  FONT_NAME=topaz.font        FONT_SIZE=8        ROW_SPACING=7
  HIGH_CONTRAST=NO            LARGE_GADGETS=NO   REDUCED_COLORS=NO
  COMPACT_MODE=AUTO           PLUGIN_TIMEOUT=30  ICON_PREVIEW=NO
  PLUGIN=PROGDIR:Plugins/Calc/Calc.plugin       (repeat)
  PLUGIN_DISABLED=...         INSTALL_DIR=SYS:Utilities/Beam68

Other files in ENVARC:Beam68: Favorites.txt, Aliases.txt, History.txt and
the Plugins drawer with plugin settings.  The index cache is
Beam68.index next to the launcher.

@endnode

@node AREXX "ARexx and Shell"
@{b}ARexx and Shell control@{ub}

ARexx port @{b}BEAM68@{ub}:

  SHOW  HIDE  RELOAD  RELOADPLUGINS  REINDEX  QUIT
  STATUS  INDEX  VERSION  PLUGINS  PLUGIN <n>  HELP

Example: @{i}rx "address BEAM68 'SHOW'"@{ui}

From the Shell: @{b}Beam68Ctl RELOAD|RELOADPLUGINS|REINDEX|SHOW|HIDE|QUIT@{ub}
@{b}Beam68Ctl STATUS@{ub} returns 0 when Beam68 runs and 5 when not;
@{b}Beam68Ctl QUITWAIT@{ub} quits and waits until it has stopped.

@{b}TIMING@{ub} reports the last search, cache-load, scan and startup times
in microseconds - useful when tuning a slow machine.

Start @{b}Beam68 SAFE@{ub} for a single start in safe mode.

@endnode

@node LANGUAGES "Languages"
@{b}Languages@{ub}

The launcher speaks the language set in the Locale preferences when a
translation exists.  Included: @{b}deutsch@{ub} and @{b}svenska@{ub}.  Catalogs
are installed in Beam68/Catalogs/<language>/Beam68.catalog; a catalog in
LOCALE:Catalogs works too.  Without a translation English is used.

Translators: start from catalogs/Beam68.cd in the source archive (the
standard CatComp/FlexCat format) and send the .ct file to the project.

Beam68Prefs and the bundled plugins have their own catalogs
(Beam68Prefs.catalog, Beam68Plugins.catalog) in LOCALE:Catalogs; Beam68Ctl
uses the launcher's catalog.  The installer follows the Locale language
too.  Deliberately left in English: ARexx replies and Beam68Ctl STATUS
output (scripts parse them), plugin command words such as "find:" or
"reboot confirm", and the weekday names of Date Utilities.

@endnode

@node SAFEMODE "Safe mode"
@{b}Safe mode@{ub}

If Beam68 crashes within its first seconds - for example because of a
broken plugin or theme - the next start runs in @{b}safe mode@{ub}: no
plugins, Workbench colours.  The start after that is normal again.
Switching the Amiga off never triggers safe mode.

Force it with @{b}Beam68 SAFE@{ub} or by creating ENV:Beam68/SafeMode.

@endnode

@node TROUBLE "Troubleshooting"
@{b}Troubleshooting@{ub}

@{b}Nothing happens when I press the hotkey.@{ub}
  Check that Beam68 runs (Exchange lists it).  Another program may use the
  same keys: choose a different hotkey on the General page.

@{b}A program is not found.@{ub}
  Is its drawer listed on the Indexing page and within the depth?  Press F2
  to rebuild the index.  "Index full" in the status line: raise MAX_ITEMS.

@{b}Opening a drawer does nothing on OS 3.1.@{ub}
  That needs workbench.library V44 (OS 3.1.4 or newer).

@{b}A plugin times out.@{ub}
  Raise the timeout on the Plugins page; after three failures a plugin is
  quarantined - use Enable/Disable to clear it.

@{b}Installing a plugin archive fails.@{ub}
  Install C:LhA or C:UnZip from Aminet, or unpack the archive and drop the
  plugin drawer on the Plugins page.

@endnode

